.TH QWCLI 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwcli \- interactive chat and single-turn query terminal runner for local Qwen3-4B
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwcli
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIprompt\fR]
[\fB\-\-rules\fR|\fB\-\-no\-rules\fR]
[\fIextra flags...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwcli
launches an interactive conversational terminal session or single-turn query powered by local Qwen3-4B.
It supports switching system prompt rules, reasoning levels, context allocations, and single-turn direct query execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " tokens"
Set context window size (16, 32, or 48 thousand tokens). Default is 32.
.TP
.BI \-r " level"
Set reasoning effort level (\fI0\fR to \fI4\fR). Default is 2.
.TP
.B \-s
Single-turn execution mode: evaluates the prompt, streams the answer, and exits cleanly.
.TP
.BI \-p " prompt"
Initial prompt text to start the session or execute with \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-rules
Enforce system instructions and security sandbox guidelines from \fIprompts/cli_rules.md\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rules
Disable system rules for unrestricted, raw model responses.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch interactive session with high reasoning:
.RS
.nf
qwcli \-r 3
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a fast single-turn query from the command line:
.RS
.nf
qwcli \-s "What is the differences between epoll and io_uring?"
.fi
.RE
